UNIT git_line
KIND FUNCTIONAL
FIDELITY package
ANCHOR rederive@4c134cacd842 cli/lsp/pr-review.mjs gitLine, driven by selfhost/seams/git_line.mjs as one mapping per requested line; cross-checked against git's own line numbering (R6)
ORACLE-CLASS deterministic
SIG git_line(text: text, lines: list[f64]) -> list[i64]
ENVELOPE text is any text (CR, LF and CRLF in any mix and position; every other character, the LINE SEPARATOR, PARAGRAPH
  SEPARATOR, NEXT LINE, form feed and vertical tab included, is ordinary). lines is a list of numbers, each any double:
  zero, negative zero, negative, fractional, beyond the text, NaN, plus or minus infinity. Nothing in the envelope throws.
DEPENDS-ON none
DESCRIPTION rederive's SIR parser counts a lone CR as a line break; git, and so GitHub's line numbers, counts only LF. For
  each requested parser line number (1-based), give the git line number (1-based) that holds that parser line's text, so a
  review note lands where GitHub shows the text. The result has one entry per entry of lines, in the same order.
BEHAVIOR
R1 BREAKS. Scan text from its start. At each position the break is taken by PINNED grammar BREAK, CR followed by LF being
  ONE break; a CR not followed by LF is a break; an LF is a break. No other character breaks. A break is LF-BEARING when it
  contains an LF (the CRLF and the LF break); the lone CR break is not.
R2 PARSER LINES. With B breaks the text has P = B + 1 parser lines, numbered 1 to P; line k is the text after break k - 1
  (the start, for k = 1) up to break k (the end of text, for k = P). The empty text has one line. A text that ends in a
  break has an empty last line. An LF then a CR is two breaks; a CR then an LF is one.
R3 GIT(k), for k from 1 to P, is 1 plus the number of LF-BEARING breaks among breaks 1 to k - 1. So GIT(1) = 1 and GIT never
  decreases; a run of lines joined by lone CRs shares one git line.
R4 FINAL is 1 plus the number of LF-BEARING breaks in the whole text. FINAL = GIT(P): a line past the end answers what the
  last parser line answers.
R5 Each entry x of lines is answered by TABLE LOOKUP (first matching row). Entries are answered independently: repeats,
  any order and the empty list are all allowed, and the empty list gives the empty list.
TABLE LOOKUP — x is the requested line, P and GIT as R2 and R3
  x is zero (negative zero included)                                       | 0 CITED FIDELITY package — the lookup table's slot 0 holds 0
  x is an integer and 1 <= x <= P                                          | GIT(x)
  anything else: an integer above P, any negative, a fraction, NaN, an infinity | FINAL CITED FIDELITY package — every key without a slot falls back to the final count
R6 Against git (the independent anchor): for every parser line k from 1 to P, git line GIT(k) holds parser line k's text, at
  the place after the lone CRs that precede it on that git line. The parser lines past git's last line are only the empty
  last line of a text ending in LF or CRLF, and the one line of the empty text (TABLE ENDINGS).
TABLE ENDINGS — G is git's line count for the text (LF count, plus 1 when the text is non-empty and does not end in LF)
  the empty text                          | P = 1; FINAL = 1, a line git does not have (G = 0)
  text ends in LF                         | last parser line empty; FINAL = G + 1, a line git does not have
  text ends in CRLF                       | last parser line empty; FINAL = G + 1, a line git does not have
  text ends in CR (not followed by LF)    | last parser line empty; FINAL = G, the git line the CR ends
  text ends in any other character        | FINAL = G
PINNED grammar BREAK = U+000D U+000A | U+000D | U+000A CITED R1 — ordered: the two-character break is preferred at a CR, so CRLF counts once
INVARIANT every answer is 0 (only for x = 0) or an integer from 1 to FINAL; GIT(k) <= k.
NOTE rust is omitted. Cause: domain — the review system ships as JavaScript (rdv review and the rederive/sir-review GitHub
  Action); there is no Rust consumer.
OUT-OF-DOMAIN outside the abstract SIG (the js file's envelope widening carries these as js-only observations): text that is
  not text (none, a number) throws; lines that is not a list (none) throws; a lines entry that is text is looked up by its
  spelling, so "2" answers GIT(2) and "02" or "x" answer FINAL.
ORACLE value -> oracles/git_line.json  CANONICAL-SHA256 0d1478cebf9c228938d7aef8cdb49052d78c6b14393e4a63cb8d621ecc16620f
SCOPE IN: R1–R6 over ENVELOPE, OUT-OF-DOMAIN as js-only observations. OUT: the review pipeline that calls gitLine (spans,
  review), rendering, and any line-break convention other than CR, LF and CRLF.
PROVENANCE rederive@4c134cacd842 (rederive, MIT), cli/lsp/pr-review.mjs export gitLine(text) returning line -> number, mapped
  over lines by selfhost/seams/git_line.mjs. Cut cold 2026-11-02 into the v0.5 contract register; anchored against git
  (git diff --no-index -U0) in anchor/git-anchor.mjs.
